    <h2>What is on the cake stand</h2>
    <p>
        There are four cakes on the counter every day, and two of them never change. The lemon drizzle is Priya’s recipe, sharp enough to make
        you squint, with a crackling sugar crust; we tried to retire it once and the neighbors would not let us. The brown butter banana loaf
        uses the bananas we buy for the café and forget about.
    </p>
    <p>
        The other two follow the season: apple and cider now, with a cider caramel, and a chocolate olive oil cake that happens to be vegan
        and is the darkest, dampest thing we bake.
    </p>

    <h2>Weekends</h2>
    <p>
        On Saturdays and Sundays there is carrot cake, with brown sugar cream cheese frosting and no raisins. We know some of you want raisins.
        We are not changing it.
    </p>

    <h2>Cake for a celebration</h2>
    <p>
        For birthdays, weddings and anything with candles, we bake whole layer cakes to order with five days’ notice. See the <a href="/cakes/">celebration cake menu</a> for flavors and sizes, or read <a href="/journal/how-to-order-a-celebration-cake/">how to
        order a celebration cake</a> before you choose.
    </p>
